1
00:00:07,921 --> 00:00:13,171
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,359 --> 00:00:15,311
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:24,901 --> 00:00:26,337
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:27,558
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:28,152 --> 00:00:33,675
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

6
00:00:34,349 --> 00:00:36,776
السلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

7
00:00:40,198 --> 00:00:44,024
Rasool Allah ﷺ held a sword in his hand,

8
00:00:45,385 --> 00:00:50,269
and he asked the Sahabah(صحابه), who will take this sword from me.

9
00:00:51,984 --> 00:00:54,587
So, the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم volunteered.

10
00:00:55,730 --> 00:00:58,326
But then Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

11
00:00:58,943 --> 00:01:02,013
Who will take this sword along with its rights.

12
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,040
So, this sword you don't just take it.

13
00:01:05,191 --> 00:01:08,544
I'm not just giving it to you, but this sword has some rights.

14
00:01:09,386 --> 00:01:13,386
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) asked Rasool Allah ﷺ; What are the rights of this sword.

15
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:18,720
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; For you to strike the enemy with it, until it bends.

16
00:01:19,821 --> 00:01:22,751
So, now the Sahabah(صحابه) were giving it a second thought,

17
00:01:22,838 --> 00:01:24,683
I mean, taking a sword until you bend it.

18
00:01:25,957 --> 00:01:30,794
But Abu Dujana رضي الله عنه came forward and said, I will, O Rasool Allah ﷺ,

19
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:31,842
 I'm going to take it,

20
00:01:32,821 --> 00:01:36,668
I'm up for that challenge,  I'll hit the enemy with it, until I bend it,

21
00:01:37,177 --> 00:01:39,365
I'm going to bend that piece of steel.

22
00:01:40,771 --> 00:01:42,813
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ gives it to him.

23
00:01:43,315 --> 00:01:45,260
Ibn Is'haaq(إبن اسحاق) says,

24
00:01:45,997 --> 00:01:52,688
When he took the sword from Rasool Allah ﷺ, he took out the red headband and put it on.

25
00:01:53,516 --> 00:01:56,811
He then began strutting about between the two lines.

26
00:01:58,043 --> 00:02:01,786
Abu Dujana(ابودجانه), when he would fight, he would put on a red headband.

27
00:02:02,618 --> 00:02:06,131
That's the sign that he's going to war.

28
00:02:06,567 --> 00:02:09,921
So, he pulls up that red headband puts it on,

29
00:02:10,543 --> 00:02:15,449
and then he starts to march in front of the army with pride.

30
00:02:16,038 --> 00:02:20,438
He's emanating this pride you can feel the strength in his walk,

31
00:02:21,991 --> 00:02:23,821
strutting in front of the enemy.

32
00:02:23,861 --> 00:02:25,228
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

33
00:02:26,115 --> 00:02:31,706
That is a way of walking that Allah dislikes, except in circumstances like this.

34
00:02:32,829 --> 00:02:35,255
Allahعَزّوجَلّ does not like this way of walking,

35
00:02:35,630 --> 00:02:38,350
but in this particular situation, Allah does like it.

36
00:02:39,586 --> 00:02:43,481
A Muslim is not supposed to be arrogant, so that's why we walk with humbleness,

37
00:02:43,756 --> 00:02:45,069
we walk with humbleness.

38
00:02:45,788 --> 00:02:48,564
Rasool Allah ﷺ would walk with humbleness,

39
00:02:48,644 --> 00:02:52,429
now we don't want this to be misunderstood as walking with weakness,

40
00:02:52,548 --> 00:02:55,387
the humbleness is something and weakness is something else.

41
00:02:55,843 --> 00:02:57,470
Rasool Allah ﷺ when he would walk,

42
00:02:58,015 --> 00:03:00,927
you can see the strength in Rasool Allah ﷺ in the way he would walk.

43
00:03:01,070 --> 00:03:02,130
 Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said;

44
00:03:02,387 --> 00:03:04,988
As if he's coming down a hill.

45
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:07,675
So, it's like firmness in walking.

46
00:03:07,996 --> 00:03:10,821
So, that's different than, we shouldn't think that

47
00:03:11,192 --> 00:03:14,188
being humble is that you're walking with weakness.

48
00:03:14,780 --> 00:03:17,869
But here Abu Dujana(ابو دجانه) is walking with pride, Khuayalaa(خُيَّلَآءْ),

49
00:03:18,835 --> 00:03:22,868
and that's not something that Allah likes, but this is done in front of the enemy.

50
00:03:23,676 --> 00:03:26,850
And that's why Allahعَزّوجَلّ likes in this particular situation.

51
00:03:27,674 --> 00:03:29,588
Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) said: And he did take it,

52
00:03:29,847 --> 00:03:31,859
referring to the sword, that he did take it

53
00:03:32,010 --> 00:03:36,678
and cleaved a path with it, through the middle of the Polytheists.

54
00:03:38,066 --> 00:03:39,431
In the middle of the Mushrikeen(مشركين)

55
00:03:39,907 --> 00:03:43,168
So, Abu Dujana(ابو دجانه) takes this sword, in order to bend it,

56
00:03:43,611 --> 00:03:48,069
he wrecks havoc in the ranks of the enemy and splits up their ranks,

57
00:03:48,362 --> 00:03:51,738
he cleaved the path with it, through the middle of Al-Mushrikeen(ألمشركين).

58
00:03:53,364 --> 00:04:00,728
Abdullah Bin Zubair(عبدالله بن الزبير), he narrates to us a story of a scene that he witnessed on the day of Uhud(أحَد).

59
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:04,827
He said, Every man he met Abu Dujana(ابو دجانه) killed.

60
00:04:05,792 --> 00:04:09,973
Among the Mushrikeen(مشركين) there was man, who executed every man he wounded.

61
00:04:10,018 --> 00:04:13,211
 Meaning this man he doesn't spare the life of anyone.

62
00:04:13,826 --> 00:04:16,769
If he meets a Muslim, A Muslim is dead.

63
00:04:18,074 --> 00:04:21,268
This man and Abu Dujana(دجانه) came ever closer to one another.

64
00:04:21,954 --> 00:04:24,418
And I pray to Allah to bring them together.

65
00:04:25,085 --> 00:04:26,147
And they did meet.

66
00:04:27,048 --> 00:04:29,099
They exchanged a couple of blows,

67
00:04:29,629 --> 00:04:32,074
the Mushrik(مشرك) then struck at Abu Dujana(ابو دجانه),

68
00:04:32,259 --> 00:04:34,397
who fended off the blow with his shield

69
00:04:34,773 --> 00:04:36,619
which trap the man sword,

70
00:04:37,007 --> 00:04:39,595
then Abu Dujana(ابو دجانه) struck and killed him.

71
00:04:40,462 --> 00:04:42,683
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) narrates a similar story,

72
00:04:42,723 --> 00:04:46,675
Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) if it's talking about the same person it could be or it could be somebody else.

73
00:04:47,402 --> 00:04:52,723
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said, I then saw one Mushrik(مشرك) heavily armored

74
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:57,668
was striking the Muslims hard and saying Come on, you sheep gathering for slaughter.

75
00:04:58,750 --> 00:05:01,079
But then I saw one Muslim fully armored,

76
00:05:01,261 --> 00:05:05,067
I mean he doesn't know this Muslim was, his armory was covering the face.

77
00:05:05,581 --> 00:05:09,264
But then I saw one Muslim fully armored waiting for him,

78
00:05:09,910 --> 00:05:13,651
and I went on over behind him and began comparing the Muslim with the Mushrik(مشرك).

79
00:05:13,755 --> 00:05:17,620
 So, Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) here saw these two men and he was sizing them up.

80
00:05:18,166 --> 00:05:20,691
He says the latter was better in equipment and form,

81
00:05:20,731 --> 00:05:26,746
meaning the Mushrik(مشرك) was bigger and stronger and he also had better equipment,

82
00:05:26,809 --> 00:05:29,648
 so you would expect that the Mushrik(مشرك) would win.

83
00:05:30,802 --> 00:05:32,910
I kept on waiting until they met.

84
00:05:33,389 --> 00:05:37,894
The Muslim then struck the unbeliever a blow with his sword on his shoulder,

85
00:05:38,501 --> 00:05:41,777
the sword came right down through, to his thigh.

86
00:05:42,518 --> 00:05:44,756
So, he struck the Mushrik(مشرك) on the shoulder

87
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:49,540
and the sword went through tearing apart his torso

88
00:05:49,950 --> 00:05:56,715
until it came out from under his thigh, cutting him into two.

89
00:05:57,526 --> 00:06:01,707
Ka'ab Ibn Malik(كعب ابن مالك) said: Then the Muslim uncovered his face and said,

90
00:06:01,873 --> 00:06:04,331
What about that Ka'ab(كعب)? I'm Abu Dujana(ابودجانه).

91
00:06:06,412 --> 00:06:09,894
So, Abu Dujana(ابودجانه) knew that Ka'ab(كعب) was watching and watching this match.

92
00:06:09,966 --> 00:06:14,356
 So, when the match was over, Abu Dujana(ابودجانه) uncovers his faces, and says,

93
00:06:14,426 --> 00:06:16,626
What about that Ka'ab(كعب), I'm Abu Dujana(ابودجانه).

94
00:06:17,116 --> 00:06:20,576
He was a proud man, and he has every right to be proud.

95
00:06:22,701 --> 00:06:27,275
The Muslims were winning, and the enemy was fleeing the battle ground.

96
00:06:28,126 --> 00:06:30,278
And the Sahabah(صحابه) said, We could see,

97
00:06:30,492 --> 00:06:34,381
the women of Arabia used to put this jewelry on their feet.

98
00:06:35,521 --> 00:06:38,824
So, they would say that we would see that jewelry on their feet

99
00:06:38,933 --> 00:06:41,373
 because they're tucking up their clothes to run away.

100
00:06:41,902 --> 00:06:45,649
So, that's it. The enemy was showing the Muslims, their backs.

101
00:06:47,894 --> 00:06:57,625
Bannu Abd-Ad-Daar(بنوعبدالدار) were the ones, who had the responsibility of holding the standard of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

102
00:06:58,075 --> 00:07:02,361
 And this was part of the Division of authorities that existed in Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

103
00:07:02,617 --> 00:07:06,214
one family would take care of feeding the pilgrims,

104
00:07:06,493 --> 00:07:08,738
one family had the key to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

105
00:07:08,952 --> 00:07:14,263
one family had the key to An-Nadwa(ألندوى), the sort of the Parliament of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

106
00:07:14,616 --> 00:07:18,219
and one family, they held the banners of war.

107
00:07:18,589 --> 00:07:20,751
So, this family was Bannu Abd-Ad-Daar(بنوعبدالدار),

108
00:07:20,838 --> 00:07:26,341
they were the ones responsible for it on Badr(بدر) and they are also responsible for it, on Uhud(أحَد).

109
00:07:27,359 --> 00:07:31,002
And I mean to show you the importance of the standard.

110
00:07:31,279 --> 00:07:36,598
You know, because probably due to modern warfare, we don't really understand what's the significance of a banner.

111
00:07:36,835 --> 00:07:38,411
That was the rallying point,

112
00:07:38,629 --> 00:07:44,398
that was the indication to the soldier that we're still in the fight and my army is here.

113
00:07:45,278 --> 00:07:47,879
Without the banner, the soldier is not going to fight anymore.

114
00:07:47,962 --> 00:07:50,912
If the banner falls down, that means that we have lost the war,

115
00:07:51,238 --> 00:07:52,861
and it's time for me to run away.

116
00:07:53,383 --> 00:07:55,744
So to show the significance of this banner issue,

117
00:07:55,784 --> 00:07:58,815
Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) told Bannu Abd-Ad-Daar(بنوعبدالدار);

118
00:07:59,490 --> 00:08:02,987
You were incharge of our banner at the Battle of Badr(بدر).

119
00:08:03,399 --> 00:08:08,431
And you saw what happened to us, men will only fight for their flags.

120
00:08:08,923 --> 00:08:11,744
If once, they are lost, they withdraw,

121
00:08:13,053 --> 00:08:18,523
either take care of our banner for us or give it over to us and we will relieve you of it.

122
00:08:19,292 --> 00:08:23,200
So, this angered them and said we give over our banner to you.

123
00:08:23,638 --> 00:08:27,741
You will learn tomorrow when we meet and in battle, how we will behave.

124
00:08:28,141 --> 00:08:29,451
So, he charged them up.

125
00:08:29,753 --> 00:08:32,427
And that was the response Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) wanted.

126
00:08:33,901 --> 00:08:35,928
So they fought under their banner well.

127
00:08:35,968 --> 00:08:42,505
I mean, Bannu Abd-Ad-Daar(بنوعبدالدار) they lost seven of their men one after the other.

128
00:08:43,652 --> 00:08:45,752
One would hold the banner that he would be killed.

129
00:08:45,832 --> 00:08:48,931
The second would come in line take it over, he would be killed,

130
00:08:48,971 --> 00:08:49,629
third,

131
00:08:49,932 --> 00:08:53,557
Seven of their men were killed carrying the banner

132
00:08:53,652 --> 00:08:55,983
 and then one of their slaves, his name is Sawaab(ثواب)

133
00:08:56,203 --> 00:09:01,139
Abyssinian slave, he took hold of it and his arms were severed,

134
00:09:01,653 --> 00:09:06,102
and he was still trying to hug the banner and then he would say, Aazart(أعذرْتْ)

135
00:09:06,538 --> 00:09:11,346
Have I done my part and he couldn't pronounce the Za(ز), it was Azart( آعزرت)

136
00:09:11,882 --> 00:09:14,559
but his Arabic wasn't perfect, so he said: Aazart(أعذرْتْ).

137
00:09:15,470 --> 00:09:19,965
Anyway so after that the banner just fell down and they left it on the ground,

138
00:09:20,559 --> 00:09:23,838
and that is when Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) started to flee the battle ground.

139
00:09:24,068 --> 00:09:25,825
 So, they were defeated, they lost

140
00:09:26,380 --> 00:09:27,519
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ said,

141
00:09:27,973 --> 00:09:35,346
وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ وَعْدَهُ إِذْ تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بِإِذْنِهِ ۖ

142
00:09:35,768 --> 00:09:38,837
And Allah had certainly fulfilled His promise to you

143
00:09:39,104 --> 00:09:41,160
when you were killing them by His permission.

144
00:09:41,516 --> 00:09:47,768
So, even according to Qur'an, the Muslims have won the battle of Uhud(أحَد) initially.

145
00:09:48,997 --> 00:09:50,363
But the tides were turning.

146
00:09:51,053 --> 00:09:58,006
The archers, who were instructed by Rasool Allah ﷺ to remain on the hill not to move,

147
00:09:58,141 --> 00:10:01,200
 if you see us winning, Do not come down until I tell you,

148
00:10:01,635 --> 00:10:06,695
if you see us losing and vultures picking off our bodies eating from our bodies,

149
00:10:06,949 --> 00:10:14,485
Do not come down until I tell you, very explicit, clear, instructions from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

150
00:10:15,269 --> 00:10:20,810
Now in the heat of battle when the emotions take over,

151
00:10:21,048 --> 00:10:24,826
sometimes the mind is obscured.

152
00:10:25,207 --> 00:10:34,114
So, what happened is, when the archers saw that the Muslims were now gathering booty, Al-Ghanaem(ألغنائم),

153
00:10:35,206 --> 00:10:37,428
they wanted to go down and join.

154
00:10:38,410 --> 00:10:40,795
But their Ameer(امير) Abdullah Bin Jubair(عبدالله بن جبير), he said,

155
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,554
Don't you remember the instructions of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

156
00:10:43,615 --> 00:10:45,917
that we shouldn't come down, until he tells us so.

157
00:10:47,101 --> 00:10:49,812
They said the battle is over and they left.

158
00:10:50,578 --> 00:10:53,953
So, out of the 50 archers, 40 of them defected.

159
00:10:54,510 --> 00:10:57,446
We're going to call this defection because that's what it is.

160
00:10:58,557 --> 00:11:03,078
They have disobeyed the order of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

161
00:11:04,180 --> 00:11:08,456
and this is a serious thing in warfare, to disobey the commander.

162
00:11:10,658 --> 00:11:14,549
Or not defected, we should call it, it was mutiny,

163
00:11:15,513 --> 00:11:16,607
so they left their post.

164
00:11:17,488 --> 00:11:22,351
Khalid Ibn Walid(خالد ابن وليد) was the head of the cavalry of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

165
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:24,817
He and Ikrimah Bin Abi Jahal(عكرمه بن ابي جهل).

166
00:11:25,881 --> 00:11:33,127
When they detected the weak point, that was exposed

167
00:11:34,266 --> 00:11:39,669
they immediately took advantage of that, and outflanked the Muslim army.

168
00:11:40,487 --> 00:11:46,069
And because the Muslims were not expecting that, and they were taken by surprise.

169
00:11:47,203 --> 00:11:49,516
It was a chaotic state for the Muslims,

170
00:11:50,170 --> 00:11:54,424
and when the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) saw that they attacked from the other side,

171
00:11:54,530 --> 00:11:55,998
so now the Muslims were sandwiched,

172
00:11:56,077 --> 00:11:59,006
they were attacked from both sides from the front and from the rear.

173
00:11:59,616 --> 00:12:03,461
And this disoriented the Muslim soldiers

174
00:12:03,833 --> 00:12:06,969
because they are fighting now in both direction

175
00:12:07,478 --> 00:12:13,082
and the ranks would became disorganized, they were not lined up properly as they should.

176
00:12:13,527 --> 00:12:16,994
 And that is when the Muslims were defeated.

177
00:12:17,455 --> 00:12:20,014
And that is when they were being killed,

178
00:12:20,490 --> 00:12:22,951
and they were falling one after the other.

179
00:12:24,014 --> 00:12:28,719
It is said that only 12 men remained around Rasool Allah ﷺ.

180
00:12:30,324 --> 00:12:31,639
Allahعزوجل says;

181
00:12:32,020 --> 00:12:39,286
وَلَقَدْ صَدَقَكُمُ اللَّهُ وَعْدَهُ إِذْ تَحُسُّونَهُمْ بِإِذْنِهِ

182
00:12:39,683 --> 00:12:51,505
حَتَّىٰ إِذَا فَشِلْتُمْ وَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ وَعَصَيْتُمْ مِنْ بَعْدِ مَا أَرَاكُمْ مَا تُحِبُّونَ۝

183
00:12:51,973 --> 00:13:00,166
مِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الدُّنْيَا وَمِنْكُمْ مَنْ يُرِيدُ الْآخِرَةَ

184
00:13:00,353 --> 00:13:07,050
ثُمَّ صَرَفَكُمْ عَنْهُمْ لِيَبْتَلِيَكُمْ وَلَقَدْ عَفَا عَنْكُمْۗ

185
00:13:07,347 --> 00:13:12,840
وَاللَّهُ ذُو فَضْلٍ عَلَى الْمُؤْمِنِينَ۝

186
00:13:13,595 --> 00:13:16,719
Allah has certainly fulfilled His promise to you,

187
00:13:16,915 --> 00:13:21,555
when you were killing them by His permission, until the time when you lost courage

188
00:13:22,453 --> 00:13:26,864
and fell to disputing about the order given by the prophet

189
00:13:26,904 --> 00:13:29,661
 and disobeyed after He had shown you

190
00:13:30,048 --> 00:13:31,772
that which you love, I mean, victory.

191
00:13:32,287 --> 00:13:36,605
After among you are some, who desire this world,

192
00:13:36,916 --> 00:13:39,476
and among you are some who desire the Hereafter.

193
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,187
Abdullah Bin Masood(عبدالله بن مسعود) said, I didn't know

194
00:13:41,467 --> 00:13:46,671
that there were some of us who loved and desire this world, until this Ayah(آية) was revealed.

195
00:13:46,711 --> 00:13:49,413
So, Qur'an was exposing what was in the hearts

196
00:13:49,676 --> 00:13:51,787
this is how Qur'an writes history,

197
00:13:51,843 --> 00:13:57,360
 it doesn't only take the outside, but it also takes the inner dimension of the soul.

198
00:13:57,685 --> 00:14:02,153
 Then Allah says, Then he turned you back from them defeated,

199
00:14:02,538 --> 00:14:03,806
 that He might test you.

200
00:14:04,234 --> 00:14:06,511
And he has already forgiven you.

201
00:14:06,702 --> 00:14:09,710
And Allah is the possessor of bounty for the believers.

202
00:14:09,821 --> 00:14:12,427
So, Allah tested the believers with victory on Badr(بدر)

203
00:14:12,467 --> 00:14:14,319
and He is now testing them with the defeat on Uhud(أحَد).

204
00:14:14,359 --> 00:14:15,747
It's all test from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

205
00:14:16,506 --> 00:14:20,116
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) said, the Muslim ranks broke

206
00:14:21,463 --> 00:14:24,108
and the enemy gained advantage over them.

207
00:14:24,795 --> 00:14:29,279
It was the day of trial and testing, in which Allah honored someone with martyrdom.

208
00:14:30,058 --> 00:14:34,190
At last the enemy broke through to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

209
00:14:34,689 --> 00:14:35,892
he was hit with a rock

210
00:14:36,372 --> 00:14:37,606
 and fell on his side,

211
00:14:37,919 --> 00:14:39,348
 breaking his front teeth,

212
00:14:39,757 --> 00:14:41,899
slashing his face and splitting his lips.

213
00:14:41,939 --> 00:14:45,214
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ himself was injured in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

214
00:14:46,328 --> 00:14:50,128
In Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ) it says that Fatima(فاطمه) was the one, who was washing him,

215
00:14:50,498 --> 00:14:53,157
and Ali(علي) poured the water from the shield.

216
00:14:53,244 --> 00:14:55,078
So, Ali(علي) was pouring the water and

217
00:14:55,322 --> 00:14:57,300
Fatima(فاطمه) was washing the wounds.

218
00:14:57,624 --> 00:15:00,483
When Fatima(فاطمه) saw that the water was only increasing the blood flow

219
00:15:00,758 --> 00:15:05,911
She took a piece of matting and she set fire to it and then attach it to the wound.

220
00:15:06,372 --> 00:15:09,688
So, over here you have, it is ashes, and it's also hot

221
00:15:10,066 --> 00:15:14,366
ashes are very dry and it would absorb the water from the wound and make it dry

222
00:15:14,763 --> 00:15:17,792
and that would prevent the blood from flowing.

223
00:15:17,974 --> 00:15:22,577
And It's also hot so it would probably disinfect the wound.

224
00:15:23,329 --> 00:15:26,747
This is mentioned in Bukhari(بخاريْ), it says that the blood seized flowing

225
00:15:27,180 --> 00:15:31,958
and his front tooth was broken that day his face was wounded

226
00:15:32,383 --> 00:15:35,524
and his helmet was crushed onto his head.

227
00:15:36,557 --> 00:15:40,451
It was Ibn Qamiyah(إبن قميه) who shot Rasool Allah ﷺ at the cheek

228
00:15:40,843 --> 00:15:47,374
and it was Utba Bin Abi Waqas(عتبةبن ابي وقاص), who hit the lip and lower tooth of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

229
00:15:47,414 --> 00:15:48,565
 Abdur Razzaq(عبدالرزاق) says,

230
00:15:49,111 --> 00:15:54,271
The Messenger of Allah spoke a curse against Utba Bin Abi Waqas(عتبة بن ابي وقاص) saying;

231
00:15:54,682 --> 00:15:57,358
O Allah may change not come to him.

232
00:15:57,644 --> 00:16:00,177
So, that he does die as an unbeliever.

233
00:16:00,605 --> 00:16:01,903
Ibn Kathir(اِبْنِ كَثِيْر) commented

234
00:16:02,354 --> 00:16:09,721
and no change did come over him so that he did die as an unbeliever bound for hellfire.

235
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:14,404
So, what was the reaction to this defeat,

236
00:16:15,421 --> 00:16:21,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ as narrated by Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه, he said,

237
00:16:22,441 --> 00:16:26,895
While Rasool was wiping the blood off his face,

238
00:16:27,425 --> 00:16:30,652
He said, How could any people prosper,

239
00:16:31,121 --> 00:16:34,976
Who struck their prophet and broke his front teeth?

240
00:16:35,279 --> 00:16:37,017
While he called people to Allah.

241
00:16:37,710 --> 00:16:39,247
How could these people prosper?

242
00:16:39,747 --> 00:16:41,042
How could they succeed?

243
00:16:41,634 --> 00:16:45,271
When they do this to the Prophet who's calling them to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

244
00:16:46,438 --> 00:16:48,403
Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية),

245
00:16:48,897 --> 00:16:58,179
لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ أَوْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ أَوْ يُعَذِّبَهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ ظَالِمُونَ۝

246
00:16:58,984 --> 00:17:03,191
Not for you, O Muhammad(محمد) but for Allah is the decision

247
00:17:03,443 --> 00:17:07,731
 whether He should cut them down or forgive them or punish them.

248
00:17:07,922 --> 00:17:09,189
For indeed they are wrongdoers.

249
00:17:09,269 --> 00:17:12,189
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying, The fate of these people is not up to you

250
00:17:13,180 --> 00:17:14,760
It's in the hands of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

251
00:17:15,301 --> 00:17:19,480
It is up to Allahعَزّوجَلّ to cut them down, or to forgive them, or to punish them.

252
00:17:20,196 --> 00:17:24,497
They deserve punishment but if Allahعَزّوجَلّ wants to forgive them, it is up to Him.

253
00:17:25,873 --> 00:17:31,441
So, this shows you that even Rasool Allah ﷺ does not control the fate of humanity.

254
00:17:31,499 --> 00:17:33,428
 It's all in the hands of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

255
00:17:33,998 --> 00:17:37,356
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is the One, Who controls, who becomes Muslim and who doesn't

256
00:17:37,392 --> 00:17:39,886
 and who should be punished and who shouldn't be punished.

257
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:42,509
So, if this right wasn't given to Rasool Allah ﷺ

258
00:17:42,929 --> 00:17:44,409
who are we to claim that right?

259
00:17:44,504 --> 00:17:46,290
It's all in the hands of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

260
00:17:47,757 --> 00:17:52,946
Some of the Muslims, when they saw the defeat,

261
00:17:53,026 --> 00:17:56,549
and when they heard the rumor that Rasool Allah ﷺ was killed

262
00:17:56,589 --> 00:18:01,137
 because this rumors spread like wildfire in the Muslim army that he was killed.

263
00:18:01,469 --> 00:18:04,471
The origin of the rumor was that he was injured,

264
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:08,973
but you know, in such a state, things could get blown out of proportion.

265
00:18:09,012 --> 00:18:13,726
So, the rumor that was going around was that Rasool Allah ﷺ was in fact killed.

266
00:18:14,107 --> 00:18:16,172
 So, how did they react to that?

267
00:18:16,844 --> 00:18:18,300
Well, some of them said,

268
00:18:18,613 --> 00:18:21,275
We'd better send an envoy to Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن ابيئ)

269
00:18:21,328 --> 00:18:23,735
and have him get us a truce from Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان).

270
00:18:24,196 --> 00:18:29,730
People! Muhammad(محمد) has been killed, go back home before they get to you and kill you.

271
00:18:30,395 --> 00:18:36,118
Here we have some Muslims, who are defeated, the defeat reached to their hearts.

272
00:18:37,124 --> 00:18:40,461
And under the pressure of the moment,

273
00:18:41,842 --> 00:18:47,626
they thought that the best course of action was to go to Abdullah Bin Obaeye(عبدالله بن ابي), the Munafiq(منافق)

274
00:18:48,068 --> 00:18:53,716
because he has good relations with Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and to ask him to bring a truce.

275
00:18:55,039 --> 00:18:56,680
And Ya'ani(يعني) Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

276
00:18:56,865 --> 00:18:58,975
The Battle of Uhud(أحَد), itself may not repeat

277
00:18:59,405 --> 00:19:02,876
but the reaction of the people can repeat in events that are similar.

278
00:19:03,495 --> 00:19:06,799
So, sometimes you'd find that when Muslims are under pressure and

279
00:19:07,197 --> 00:19:12,735
when they feel that they could be defeated in battle,

280
00:19:13,423 --> 00:19:17,220
you can have some people who would now think well, why don't I go to the government's

281
00:19:17,300 --> 00:19:23,304
and ask them to help me or why don't I go to the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ and let's have a truce with them.

282
00:19:23,534 --> 00:19:24,930
This is a sign of weakness.

283
00:19:25,565 --> 00:19:29,950
But the Muslims, who had strong Eeman(ايمان) in their hearts, what was their reaction?

284
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:34,053
One of Al-Muhajiroon(المهاجرون) said that he passed by one of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)

285
00:19:35,010 --> 00:19:37,184
a man, who was covered in his own blood,

286
00:19:37,224 --> 00:19:39,248
He was soaked in his own blood and asked him.

287
00:19:39,477 --> 00:19:41,787
Are you aware that Muhammad(محمد) has been killed.

288
00:19:42,070 --> 00:19:45,234
The Ansaari(انصاري) responded if Muhammad(محمد) has been killed

289
00:19:45,748 --> 00:19:50,344
then he must have fulfilled his mission, so fight on for your religion.

290
00:19:50,753 --> 00:19:53,776
Let's die as he died fighting for Islam.

291
00:19:55,046 --> 00:19:58,589
So, these are Muslims, who cannot be defeated in their hearts,

292
00:19:58,644 --> 00:20:00,573
 even if they're defeated on the battleground,

293
00:20:01,802 --> 00:20:04,123
defeat will never get into their spirit.

294
00:20:04,668 --> 00:20:06,304
They will always have commitment

295
00:20:06,384 --> 00:20:09,985
and this is, what is called in Islam thabaat(ثبات) steadfast.

296
00:20:10,620 --> 00:20:16,684
Never would such a Muslim try to negotiate with the enemy of Allahعَزّوجَلّ

297
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:21,125
 or ask the Munafiqeen(منافقين), to appeal and intercede for them.

298
00:20:21,792 --> 00:20:25,911
Fine, if Rasool Allah ﷺ was killed, we're gonna die like he was.

299
00:20:27,236 --> 00:20:32,777
And this is the steadfastness that we should learn from the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

300
00:20:34,968 --> 00:20:36,410
The Muslims had to retreat,

301
00:20:36,734 --> 00:20:39,949
so Rasool Allah ﷺ was trying to organize that retreat,

302
00:20:40,013 --> 00:20:44,381
but retreats could be catastrophic if they are not commanded well.

303
00:20:44,753 --> 00:20:49,054
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ wants to organize this retreat

304
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:52,217
and to protect themselves while they are retreating.

305
00:20:52,297 --> 00:20:56,892
So, the enemy now was gaining the upper hand and was attacking in full force

306
00:20:57,199 --> 00:20:59,304
and they were getting closer to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

307
00:20:59,384 --> 00:21:00,602
So, Rasool Ullah asked,

308
00:21:01,095 --> 00:21:05,677
He said, Whoever will repel them, will be my companion in paradise.

309
00:21:06,108 --> 00:21:08,174
I mean, that's how difficult the situation was,

310
00:21:08,214 --> 00:21:10,128
Rasool Ullah was promising paradise

311
00:21:10,341 --> 00:21:15,912
to the one, who will succeed in stopping the attacks of the kuffar(كفار) that were reaching him.

312
00:21:16,987 --> 00:21:18,919
So, one of Al-Ansaar(الانصار) volunteered

313
00:21:19,458 --> 00:21:24,744
and he would fire his arrows at the enemy until he was killed.

314
00:21:25,173 --> 00:21:28,301
So Rasool Allah ﷺ asks for a volunteer another time,

315
00:21:28,650 --> 00:21:31,594
 another Ansari(انصاري) comes up, he's also killed

316
00:21:32,031 --> 00:21:35,406
and a third time, a third Ansaari(انصاري) would stand up

317
00:21:35,485 --> 00:21:36,208
and then a fourth

318
00:21:36,241 --> 00:21:38,224
and the fifth and every time they're killed,

319
00:21:38,311 --> 00:21:40,882
 so this in addition to the sacrifice of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار),

320
00:21:40,930 --> 00:21:47,371
can also show you the disastrous effect this attack of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) was having,

321
00:21:47,422 --> 00:21:55,629
it was a strong attack, until seven of Al-Ansaar(الانصار) died under Rasool Allah ﷺ.

322
00:21:56,044 --> 00:21:56,964
Allah u Akbar(الله اكبر).

323
00:21:57,471 --> 00:22:02,105
Seven bodies, laying under the feet of Rasool Allah ﷺ, to defend him.

324
00:22:02,786 --> 00:22:04,675
And that's why they were called Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)

325
00:22:04,715 --> 00:22:06,674
and you're going to hear me repeat this again and again.

326
00:22:06,714 --> 00:22:08,067
That's why they're called Ansaar(انصار)

327
00:22:08,553 --> 00:22:13,393
they didn't receive this title, this honor of being Ansaar(انصار),

328
00:22:13,643 --> 00:22:16,766
 which is given to them in Qur'an and by Rasool Allah ﷺ,

329
00:22:17,077 --> 00:22:19,745
they didn't get that out of nothing, they earned it.

330
00:22:21,634 --> 00:22:29,283
You have seven young men, dead under the feet of Rasool Allah ﷺ defending him, giving their lives for him.

331
00:22:30,085 --> 00:22:31,370
May Allah be pleased with them.

332
00:22:32,834 --> 00:22:35,133
In Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ), Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) says,

333
00:22:35,498 --> 00:22:40,354
I never heard the Prophet of Allah swear by both his parents to anyone

334
00:22:40,815 --> 00:22:44,127
except Saad Ibn Malik(سعدابن مالك), or Saad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعدابن ابي وقاص).

335
00:22:45,170 --> 00:22:47,715
At Uhud(أحَد) I heard him say; Sa'ad(سعد) shoot

336
00:22:48,391 --> 00:22:52,642
May my father and my mother be your ransom. Allah U Akbar(الله اكبر)

337
00:22:54,530 --> 00:22:56,859
This Dua(دعا) for Saad Ibn Malik(سعدابن مالك)

338
00:22:56,993 --> 00:23:01,096
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying; May my father and mother be your ransom O Sa'ad(سعد).

339
00:23:02,940 --> 00:23:09,671
That is how pleased Rasool Allah ﷺ was with the performance of Saad Ibn Abi Waqasرضي الله عنه.

340
00:23:11,349 --> 00:23:20,185
And another hero next to Rasool Allah ﷺ, standing next to him and defending him, was Talha Bin Ubaidellah رضي الله عنه.

341
00:23:21,313 --> 00:23:27,613
At the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) and this is narrated by Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) in Musnad Imam Ahmad(مسند امام احمد)

342
00:23:28,493 --> 00:23:29,776
He said that at the Battle of Uhud(أحَد),

343
00:23:30,014 --> 00:23:36,921
Abu Talha(ابوطلحه) was shooting directly in front of Rasool Allah ﷺ, who was shielding himself behind him.

344
00:23:37,919 --> 00:23:42,842
As he shot the Messenger of Allah would raise himself up to see where the arrows would strike.

345
00:23:43,687 --> 00:23:48,543
At this Abu Talha(ابوطلحه) would say as he brought his chest up to its full height,

346
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:54,297
Let it be so, May my father and my mother be your ransom or messenger of Allah

347
00:23:54,614 --> 00:23:59,554
no arrow will hit you, my chest will be in the way of yours.

348
00:24:00,009 --> 00:24:00,862
لا اله الا الله

349
00:24:02,235 --> 00:24:04,987
And he would also say I am sturdy O Messenger of Allah

350
00:24:05,395 --> 00:24:09,188
direct me according to your needs and order me to do, whatever you want.

351
00:24:11,537 --> 00:24:14,223
These were the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

352
00:24:16,259 --> 00:24:20,672
Rasool Allah ﷺ retreated to the mountain of Uhud(أحَد) itself

353
00:24:21,335 --> 00:24:24,988
in a crevice in the mountain, that's where he withdrew to.

354
00:24:25,876 --> 00:24:27,975
climbing up the mountain was difficult for him.

355
00:24:28,015 --> 00:24:31,512
So Talha(طلحه) had to carry him because Rasool Allah ﷺ was injured.

356
00:24:32,476 --> 00:24:36,836
And when they climbed up the mountain, that is when the battle stopped

357
00:24:36,916 --> 00:24:40,957
because Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) dared not to pursue the Muslims up the mountain.

358
00:24:41,710 --> 00:24:45,196
And plus the cavalry cannot fight in such terrain.

359
00:24:45,577 --> 00:24:53,152
So, it would have to be the foot soldiers and this was something the enemy wasn't ready or prepared to do.

360
00:24:54,181 --> 00:24:58,630
So, now Rasool Allah ﷺ and the Muslims were up in the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

361
00:24:59,719 --> 00:25:05,003
And Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) approaches them, and he calls to them.

362
00:25:05,115 --> 00:25:05,621
 He said,

363
00:25:06,256 --> 00:25:07,907
Is Muhammad(محمد) alive.

364
00:25:08,728 --> 00:25:10,451
And he hears no answer.

365
00:25:11,233 --> 00:25:14,097
He then asks, Is Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) alive?

366
00:25:14,815 --> 00:25:15,855
 No response.

367
00:25:16,356 --> 00:25:17,607
Is Umar(عُمَر) alive.

368
00:25:17,802 --> 00:25:18,842
 No response.

369
00:25:19,435 --> 00:25:24,460
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) is now happy and he told his people that these men have been killed.

370
00:25:25,410 --> 00:25:29,349
Now Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) couldn't stand hearing Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) say that.

371
00:25:29,417 --> 00:25:30,261
So he said,

372
00:25:30,589 --> 00:25:35,185
The three men whom you mentioned are alive to upset you.

373
00:25:36,356 --> 00:25:38,741
So, Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) responded back, he said,

374
00:25:39,531 --> 00:25:41,321
A battle for the Battle of Badr(بدر),

375
00:25:41,537 --> 00:25:42,993
warfare goes in cycles,

376
00:25:43,073 --> 00:25:45,341
meaning one day you win, one day we win.

377
00:25:46,251 --> 00:25:49,364
And you will find some bodies mutilated

378
00:25:49,798 --> 00:25:52,653
I did not order that, but it didn't bother me.

379
00:25:53,856 --> 00:25:56,872
Raise up Hubal(حبل), Raise up Hubal(حبل) and he started chanting,

380
00:25:57,360 --> 00:25:58,476
Raise up Hubal(حبل).

381
00:25:59,002 --> 00:26:00,175
So Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

382
00:26:00,348 --> 00:26:01,894
Aren't you gonna respond back.

383
00:26:01,949 --> 00:26:03,100
They said, What should we say?

384
00:26:03,195 --> 00:26:04,075
He said, Say

385
00:26:04,282 --> 00:26:06,308
Allah is higher and more glorious

386
00:26:06,348 --> 00:26:09,544
and this rhymes with what Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), said,

387
00:26:09,584 --> 00:26:09,933
He said,

388
00:26:09,996 --> 00:26:10,922
أُعْلُوْا هُبَلْ

389
00:26:11,002 --> 00:26:12,041
Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

390
00:26:12,375 --> 00:26:14,259
اَلله اَعْلى وَ اَجَلْ

391
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:16,664
Allah is higher and more glorious.

392
00:26:16,759 --> 00:26:19,029
Hubal(حبل) by the way is one of their idols.

393
00:26:19,282 --> 00:26:20,038
He said,

394
00:26:20,232 --> 00:26:22,146
لَنَا الْعُزَّى وَلَاعُزَّى لَكُمْ

395
00:26:22,218 --> 00:26:23,916
We have Al-Uzza(عزى), another idol,

396
00:26:24,271 --> 00:26:25,749
and you have no Uzza(عزى).

397
00:26:26,255 --> 00:26:28,765
Rasool Allah ﷺ told them to respond by saying,

398
00:26:29,083 --> 00:26:31,108
 اَللهُ مَوْلَانَا وَلَامَوْلَى لَكُمْ

399
00:26:31,408 --> 00:26:34,366
Allah is our master, and you have no master.

400
00:26:36,955 --> 00:26:43,349
Allah describes the climbing of the Muslims up the mountain of Uhud(أحَد).

401
00:26:43,603 --> 00:26:44,827
 Allahعَزّوجَلّsays,

402
00:26:45,237 --> 00:26:54,712
إِذْ تُصْعِدُونَ وَلَا تَلْوُونَ عَلَىٰ أَحَدٍ وَالرَّسُولُ يَدْعُوكُمْ فِي أُخْرَاكُمْ

403
00:26:55,375 --> 00:27:05,601
وَالرَّسُولُ يَدْعُوكُمْ فِي أُخْرَاكُمْ فَأَثَابَكُمْ غَمًّا بِغَمٍّ لِكَيْلَا تَحْزَنُوا

404
00:27:06,287 --> 00:27:12,602
لِكَيْلَا تَحْزَنُوا عَلَىٰ مَا فَاتَكُمْ وَلَا مَا أَصَابَكُمْ ۗ

405
00:27:12,932 --> 00:27:17,615
وَاللَّهُ خَبِيرٌ بِمَا تَعْمَلُونَ۝

406
00:27:18,011 --> 00:27:22,755
Remember when you fled and climb the mountain without looking aside at anyone,

407
00:27:23,311 --> 00:27:26,325
while the Messenger of Allah was calling you from behind.

408
00:27:27,110 --> 00:27:30,613
So, Allah repaid you with distress upon distress

409
00:27:31,059 --> 00:27:35,395
as you would not grieve for that which has, had escaped you

410
00:27:36,656 --> 00:27:39,573
or for that which had befallen you.

411
00:27:40,279 --> 00:27:43,363
And Allah is fully acquainted with what you do.

412
00:27:44,343 --> 00:27:45,730
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ, also says,

413
00:27:46,101 --> 00:27:56,333
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَلَّوْا مِنْكُمْ يَوْمَ الْتَقَى الْجَمْعَانِ إِنَّمَا اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ

414
00:27:56,726 --> 00:28:02,310
إِنَّمَا اسْتَزَلَّهُمُ الشَّيْطَانُ بِبَعْضِ مَا كَسَبُوا ۖ

415
00:28:02,467 --> 00:28:10,557
 وَلَقَدْ عَفَا اللَّهُ عَنْهُمْ ۗ إِنَّ اللَّهَ غَفُورٌ حَلِيمٌ۝

416
00:28:11,302 --> 00:28:15,822
Indeed, those of you, who turned back on the day, two armies met at Uhud(أحَد),

417
00:28:16,234 --> 00:28:18,453
 It was Satan who cause them to slip

418
00:28:18,870 --> 00:28:21,780
because some blame they had earned.

419
00:28:22,190 --> 00:28:24,802
But Allah has already forgiven them.

420
00:28:25,211 --> 00:28:27,301
Indeed, Allah is forgiving and forbearing.

421
00:28:27,381 --> 00:28:32,770
So, Allah is saying that what happened to you on Uhud(أحَد) is because of your sins, is because of Shaytan(شيطان).

422
00:28:33,469 --> 00:28:37,222
And we'll get into this when we talk about lessons from the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

423
00:28:37,849 --> 00:28:39,001
Allahعَزّوجَلّ also says,

424
00:28:39,041 --> 00:28:41,784
and By the way, all of these Ayaat(آيات) are from Surat Al-Imran(سورة ألعمران)

425
00:28:42,087 --> 00:28:45,986
قُلْ إِنَّ الْأَمْرَ كُلَّهُ لِلَّهِ

426
00:28:46,256 --> 00:28:51,579
يُخْفُونَ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ مَا لَا يُبْدُونَ لَكَ

427
00:28:52,047 --> 00:28:59,284
يَقُولُونَ لَوْ كَانَ لَنَا مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ مَا قُتِلْنَا هَاهُنَا

428
00:28:59,611 --> 00:29:08,721
قُلْ لَوْ كُنْتُمْ فِي بُيُوتِكُمْ لَبَرَزَ الَّذِينَ كُتِبَ عَلَيْهِمُ الْقَتْلُ إِلَىٰ مَضَاجِعِهِمْ ۖ

429
00:29:09,005 --> 00:29:16,185
وَلِيَبْتَلِيَ اللَّهُ مَا فِي صُدُورِكُمْ وَلِيُمَحِّصَ مَا فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ ۗ

430
00:29:16,495 --> 00:29:20,984
وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُورِ۝

431
00:29:21,353 --> 00:29:25,081
Say, indeed the matter belongs completely to Allah

432
00:29:25,720 --> 00:29:29,251
they conceal within themselves, what they do not reveal to you.

433
00:29:29,701 --> 00:29:33,760
They say; If there was anything we could have done in the matter

434
00:29:34,081 --> 00:29:37,075
we would have not been killed right here.

435
00:29:37,138 --> 00:29:38,532
This is what the Munafiqeen(منافقين) were saying.

436
00:29:39,102 --> 00:29:42,152
Say even if you had been inside your houses,

437
00:29:42,549 --> 00:29:47,727
those decreed to be killed, would have come out to their death beds.

438
00:29:48,833 --> 00:29:52,381
It was so that Allah might test, what is in your breasts

439
00:29:52,703 --> 00:29:54,694
and purify what is in your hearts

440
00:29:55,071 --> 00:29:58,581
and Allah is knowing of that within the breasts.

441
00:29:59,213 --> 00:30:00,604
The Munafiqeen(منافقين) were saying,

442
00:30:01,303 --> 00:30:03,625
Why did we get this ourselves into this trouble?

443
00:30:03,700 --> 00:30:04,789
Why are we fighting Jihad(جهاد)?

444
00:30:04,829 --> 00:30:06,139
Why are we doing this?

445
00:30:06,621 --> 00:30:10,271
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ is saying that you weren't killed because you went out to Jihad(جهاد),

446
00:30:10,336 --> 00:30:12,388
you were killed, because that was the Qadar(قدر) of Allah

447
00:30:12,428 --> 00:30:14,741
and if you stayed home you would also be killed.

448
00:30:15,118 --> 00:30:19,074
So, those who blame the death of Muslims on the Mujahideen(مجاهدين)

449
00:30:19,133 --> 00:30:22,634
and, the ones who are fighting for the defense of the Ummah(امة) are wrong

450
00:30:22,674 --> 00:30:25,655
and they are following the footsteps of the Munafiqeen(منافقين).

451
00:30:26,194 --> 00:30:27,477
When it comes to death

452
00:30:27,855 --> 00:30:32,916
It is a decree of Allah عَزّوجَلّ that you would die whenever your time comes.

453
00:30:33,607 --> 00:30:36,515
And it doesn't make a difference, if you go out or stay at home.

454
00:30:36,881 --> 00:30:39,302
You will die when Allah wills you to die.

455
00:30:39,731 --> 00:30:42,761
So, the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) was a test from Allahعَزّوجَلّ for them.

456
00:30:43,340 --> 00:30:46,662
Don't blame Uhud(أحَد) for the deaths of the Muslims.

457
00:30:48,516 --> 00:30:53,946
This session, or the rest of the session will be about Ash-Shahada(ألشهداء).

458
00:30:55,222 --> 00:30:59,566
There were 70 Ash-Shahada(ألشهداء), Shaheeds on the day of Uhud(أحَد).

459
00:31:00,768 --> 00:31:06,600
So, this was one of the standing points of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) is the story of Shahadah(شهادة).

460
00:31:07,303 --> 00:31:10,994
It was in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد), that 70 Muslims died as Shaheed(شهيد).

461
00:31:11,955 --> 00:31:16,232
It was in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) that the Ayaat(آيات) of Shahadah(شهادة) were revealed.

462
00:31:16,633 --> 00:31:21,694
And it was in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد) that many of the Ahadees(أحاديث) talking about Ash-Shahada(ألشهداء) were stated.

463
00:31:22,639 --> 00:31:28,569
 The Syed(سيد) of the Shahada(ألشهداء) also died in the Battle of Uhud(أحَد)

464
00:31:28,700 --> 00:31:31,045
and that's Hamzah Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه

465
00:31:31,085 --> 00:31:34,616
and when we're using the word die and dead here with Shahadah(شهادة),

466
00:31:34,877 --> 00:31:38,928
it is not the right word to use but we're using it

467
00:31:39,008 --> 00:31:43,829
and I hope that you understand the meaning that really Shaheed(شهيد) is not dead according to Qur'an.

468
00:31:44,555 --> 00:31:48,083
But This is the linguistic term that is used to refer to them,

469
00:31:48,345 --> 00:31:50,853
 but it's not really accurate

470
00:31:51,341 --> 00:31:52,999
because the Shaheed(شهيد) is alive.

471
00:31:53,782 --> 00:31:58,804
Two of the Tabaeen(تابعين) went to visit Wahshee(وحشي), who was old at that time.

472
00:31:59,471 --> 00:32:05,703
And they wanted to hear from him the story of him, killing Hamzah Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه.

473
00:32:07,824 --> 00:32:09,719
Wahshee(وحشي) said, I will tell you this story

474
00:32:10,049 --> 00:32:13,850
I will narrate the story to you as I narrated it to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

475
00:32:15,890 --> 00:32:23,972
He said, Shall I tell it to you, Just as I did to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he asked me about it.

476
00:32:24,630 --> 00:32:26,592
 I was a slave of Jubair Bin Mut'em(جبير بن مطعم),

477
00:32:27,199 --> 00:32:32,148
who's uncle was Tu'aimah Bin Udae(طعيمة بن عدي), who was struck down at Badr(بدر).

478
00:32:32,943 --> 00:32:35,491
When Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) went forth to Uhud(أحَد), Jubair(جبير) told me

479
00:32:35,919 --> 00:32:40,205
if you kill Hamza(حمزه), Muhammad(محمد)'s uncle in retaliation for my uncle's death

480
00:32:40,582 --> 00:32:41,985
then he will be a free man.

481
00:32:43,433 --> 00:32:46,076
So, I went out with the Warriors, I was an Abyssinian

482
00:32:46,445 --> 00:32:48,609
and could throw the spear like my countrymen.

483
00:32:48,649 --> 00:32:49,859
He was pretty good at it.

484
00:32:50,213 --> 00:32:51,605
I really missed with it.

485
00:32:52,159 --> 00:32:53,814
When the forces met in battle,

486
00:32:53,894 --> 00:32:57,144
I went forth looking for Hamza(حمزه) to lie, in wait for him.

487
00:32:57,802 --> 00:33:01,183
I found him right amidst affray, like an enormous camel

488
00:33:01,609 --> 00:33:04,167
striking out viciously at our men with his sword.

489
00:33:04,477 --> 00:33:06,083
Nothing would standing him.

490
00:33:07,643 --> 00:33:11,282
I made use of bushes and rocks to get close to him,

491
00:33:11,686 --> 00:33:15,807
but Saba'a Bin Abdul Uzza(سباع بن عبد العزى) got to him before me.

492
00:33:16,817 --> 00:33:19,156
When Hamza(حمزه) saw him, he said, Come over here,

493
00:33:19,610 --> 00:33:22,090
you son of a woman who does circumcisions.

494
00:33:23,402 --> 00:33:27,836
He then struck him a blow so quickly that it appeared to have missed his head.

495
00:33:29,329 --> 00:33:33,108
he then struck him a blow so quickly that appeared to have missed his head.

496
00:33:33,167 --> 00:33:38,722
I mean, the only way he recognized that I didn't miss is that the head flew off.

497
00:33:40,250 --> 00:33:45,492
I aimed my spear carefully, And when sure of it, I herd it at him.

498
00:33:46,311 --> 00:33:50,006
It struck him below his navel, and emerged between his legs.

499
00:33:50,612 --> 00:33:53,379
He tried to move towards me, but was overcome,

500
00:33:53,945 --> 00:33:55,801
I left him with a spear until he died.

501
00:33:56,527 --> 00:33:57,765
Then I went over to him,

502
00:33:57,805 --> 00:34:01,903
Subhan Allah(سبحان الله), I mean he was even terrified of Hamza(حمزه) when the spear has already struck him.

503
00:34:03,495 --> 00:34:07,511
And then I went over to him retrieved my spear

504
00:34:07,670 --> 00:34:09,416
 and returned to camp where I stayed,

505
00:34:09,992 --> 00:34:12,145
I had no business with anyone other than him.

506
00:34:12,514 --> 00:34:14,221
I only killed him to gain my freedom.

507
00:34:14,749 --> 00:34:17,415
I didn't join the battle after I killed Hamza(حمزه).

508
00:34:17,455 --> 00:34:22,968
That's it, I went back to base because that's the reason why I came to get my freedom by killing Hamza(حمزه).

509
00:34:24,198 --> 00:34:27,321
Rasool Allah ﷺ heard of the news of the death of his uncle.

510
00:34:28,444 --> 00:34:33,074
And we cannot imagine, how devastating that was to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

511
00:34:33,120 --> 00:34:35,605
I mean, this was his uncle, He loved him so much,

512
00:34:36,182 --> 00:34:39,944
it was one of the sad moments in the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

513
00:34:40,935 --> 00:34:43,397
And Rasool Ullah asked, he said:

514
00:34:43,714 --> 00:34:47,938
Did anyone see the death spot of my uncle, where is he?

515
00:34:48,536 --> 00:34:50,969
So one of the Sahabah(صحابه) volunteered and he said, I did Rasool Allah.

516
00:34:51,031 --> 00:34:52,406
 So, they went together,

517
00:34:53,267 --> 00:34:56,960
and when Rasool Allah ﷺ saw him, he cried and he choked.

518
00:34:58,030 --> 00:35:02,166
And when he saw him, His stomach was opened

519
00:35:03,024 --> 00:35:05,815
and his insides were pulled out.

520
00:35:06,454 --> 00:35:10,902
So, the man who took Rasool Allah ﷺ there, he said: "In the name of Allah, he was mutilated,

521
00:35:10,942 --> 00:35:13,684
 meaning is not the state I saw him in, when he was killed.

522
00:35:13,724 --> 00:35:17,952
I mean this mutilation didn't happened to him, when he was killed.

523
00:35:17,992 --> 00:35:19,786
 This is something that happened later on.

524
00:35:20,145 --> 00:35:26,799
And this is when, Hind Bint Ut'ba(هند بنت عتبة), the wife of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) wanted to eat the liver of Hamza(حمزه),

525
00:35:27,116 --> 00:35:29,727
 and she ordered that his liver be pulled out.

526
00:35:30,479 --> 00:35:33,592
So, this is the state in which Rasool Allah ﷺ saw his Uncle in.

527
00:35:34,238 --> 00:35:37,690
So, you can only imagine how sad Rasool Allah ﷺ was.

528
00:35:38,628 --> 00:35:43,580
And later on, Wahshee(وحشي) goes on narrating the story,

529
00:35:43,620 --> 00:35:44,929
 he said, I went back to Makkah

530
00:35:45,394 --> 00:35:49,610
but then Rasool Allah ﷺ opened Makkah, so I had to leave.

531
00:35:49,954 --> 00:35:55,795
He said, When I reached Makkah and remained, there until the Messenger of Allah conquered Makkah.

532
00:35:56,286 --> 00:35:58,482
I then fled to Taef(طائف) where I stayed.

533
00:35:59,140 --> 00:36:03,142
When the Taef(طائف) delegation left to see Rasool Allah ﷺ and to accept Islam.

534
00:36:03,182 --> 00:36:04,392
 I didn't know what to do.

535
00:36:04,627 --> 00:36:06,356
I mean, now Taef(طائف) is going to become Muslim.

536
00:36:06,396 --> 00:36:07,591
Where can I go.

537
00:36:08,477 --> 00:36:11,985
I told people, I'll go to Syria or Yemen or some other country,

538
00:36:12,413 --> 00:36:15,450
I was in the state of indecision and anxiety.

539
00:36:15,834 --> 00:36:17,697
When someone told me Come on now.

540
00:36:17,913 --> 00:36:22,659
I swear, He'll not kill anyone, who has adopted his religion and testified to the truth.

541
00:36:22,746 --> 00:36:29,886
 So, the news of the forbearance and the helm(حلم) of Rasool Allah ﷺ was all over, his forgiveness and his mercy.

542
00:36:30,209 --> 00:36:33,850
 So, this man is telling Wahshee(وحشي) that if you become Muslim, he's not going to harm you.

543
00:36:34,753 --> 00:36:35,766
When he told me that,

544
00:36:35,920 --> 00:36:42,205
I went to Rasool Allah ﷺ in Madina surprising him by standing before him and speaking testimony of truth.

545
00:36:43,093 --> 00:36:44,862
When he saw me he said, are you Wahshee(وحشي)?

546
00:36:44,927 --> 00:36:47,141
I replied: Yes, O Messenger of Allah.

547
00:36:47,513 --> 00:36:51,043
He then said, sit down and relate to me how you killed Hamza(حمزه).

548
00:36:51,998 --> 00:36:54,561
So, I related it as I did to you both.

549
00:36:55,187 --> 00:36:56,203
When I finished my account.

550
00:36:56,243 --> 00:37:00,483
He said, Wahshee(وحشي) , Can you remove your face from me.

551
00:37:01,733 --> 00:37:05,475
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want to see the face of Wahshee(وحشي) again,

552
00:37:05,530 --> 00:37:08,673
because it will bring back memories of his uncle.

553
00:37:08,962 --> 00:37:10,195
 He said, I don't want to see your face again.

554
00:37:11,398 --> 00:37:12,864
Can you keep your face away from me.

555
00:37:14,448 --> 00:37:17,349
Wahshee(وحشي) said: so I used to avoid Rasool Allah ﷺ

556
00:37:17,789 --> 00:37:20,613
wherever he might be, so that he would not see me.

557
00:37:21,101 --> 00:37:25,751
And eventually Allah Almighty and glorious is He, took him to Himself.

558
00:37:27,144 --> 00:37:35,159
Wahshee(وحشي) later on, joined in the army that went to fight with Muselma Al-Kazzab(مسيلمه الكذاب),

559
00:37:35,517 --> 00:37:37,920
 The man who claimed to be a prophet.

560
00:37:38,754 --> 00:37:43,424
Wahshee(وحشي) said, I took the spear with which I killed Hamza(حمزه).

561
00:37:44,214 --> 00:37:48,871
And when the forces met, I saw Muselemah(مسيلمه) standing with sword in hand.

562
00:37:49,677 --> 00:37:54,538
So, he was preparing to attack Muselemah(مسيلمه),

563
00:37:54,962 --> 00:37:58,287
he said, While from, on other side, there was another Muslim

564
00:37:59,029 --> 00:38:01,221
trying to attack Muselemah(مسيلمه).

565
00:38:01,882 --> 00:38:04,810
Wahshee(وحشي) with his spear and the other Muslim with his sword.

566
00:38:05,823 --> 00:38:08,359
So, I steadied my spear, until I felt good about it

567
00:38:08,767 --> 00:38:10,797
and then I let it loose on him and he struck him.

568
00:38:11,604 --> 00:38:14,832
While the other Muslim attacked from the other side

569
00:38:15,383 --> 00:38:18,105
and hit Muselemah(مسيلمه) with his sword and killed him.

570
00:38:18,765 --> 00:38:21,817
So, it was Wahshee(وحشي), who struck him first

571
00:38:22,464 --> 00:38:24,653
and then the other Muslim struck him next.

572
00:38:25,043 --> 00:38:28,650
So, Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم), Who is the one, who really killed him.

573
00:38:29,590 --> 00:38:32,610
And who was that other Muslim, It was Abu Dujana رضي الله عنه,

574
00:38:33,906 --> 00:38:35,408
the hero of the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

575
00:38:36,336 --> 00:38:37,733
Wahshee(وحشي) would say,

576
00:38:38,031 --> 00:38:39,917
If it was I who killed him,

577
00:38:40,123 --> 00:38:42,123
then I killed the best of men,

578
00:38:42,461 --> 00:38:44,274
and I also kills the worst of them.

579
00:38:44,853 --> 00:38:49,848
I killed the uncle of Muhammadﷺ and then I also killed Muselma Al-Kazzab(مسيلمه الكذاب).

580
00:38:50,701 --> 00:38:52,994
It is mentioned that Rasool Allah ﷺ told Wahshee(وحشي)

581
00:38:53,656 --> 00:38:58,877
go and fight in the path of Allah, as you fought against the religion of Allah.

582
00:38:59,773 --> 00:39:03,032
And that is how it is, in Islam if you commit a sin

583
00:39:03,552 --> 00:39:07,204
 try to erase it by performing a good deed.

584
00:39:07,300 --> 00:39:09,847
إنَّ الْحَسَنَاتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّئَاتِ

585
00:39:10,230 --> 00:39:12,498
Good deeds erase the evil ones.

586
00:39:13,153 --> 00:39:15,073
So, whenever you have committed a sin,

587
00:39:15,307 --> 00:39:20,578
 try to make up for that sin by doing good deeds, in order to erase it, and to wipe it away.

588
00:39:21,288 --> 00:39:22,241
I mean, Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب).

589
00:39:22,808 --> 00:39:25,431
He said about his argument with Rasool Allah ﷺ

590
00:39:25,508 --> 00:39:27,415
and he felt that, that was something wrong to do.

591
00:39:27,746 --> 00:39:28,064
So, he said;

592
00:39:28,104 --> 00:39:31,871
مَا زِلْتُ بَعْدَ ذَالِكْ تَصَدَّقْ وَ أعتق الرَّقَابْ وَاَصُوْمْ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ الله

593
00:39:32,057 --> 00:39:35,262
After that I remained fasting and giving charity

594
00:39:35,601 --> 00:39:39,129
and praying at night to wipe away that sin.

595
00:39:39,675 --> 00:39:43,238
So, this is how, you should approach your sins and this is part of Touba(توبة).

596
00:39:43,639 --> 00:39:47,985
Do good deeds with the intention of erasing your sins.

597
00:39:49,219 --> 00:39:53,221
And this is the month of forgiveness, we don't want to forget to ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to forgive us all.

598
00:39:53,261 --> 00:39:54,998
 O Allah عَزّوجَلّ have your mercy on us

599
00:39:55,423 --> 00:39:57,240
and forgive us all in this blessed month.

600
00:39:58,686 --> 00:40:05,298
Rasool Allah ﷺ saw, a woman after the battle was over rushing towards the bodies of the dead.

601
00:40:06,122 --> 00:40:10,343
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told Az-Zubair(ألزبير) to go and stop that woman

602
00:40:10,624 --> 00:40:14,401
Az-Zubair(ألزبير) said: I felt that, that woman was my mother Safiyah(صفيه),

603
00:40:14,441 --> 00:40:19,173
 Saffiyah Bint Abdul Muttalib(صفيه بنت عبدالمطلب), the aunt of Rasool Allah ﷺ, she was his Aunt.

604
00:40:19,733 --> 00:40:22,141
So, he rushes towards her and he stops her

605
00:40:22,895 --> 00:40:25,775
She pushes him in his chest and said move away

606
00:40:26,134 --> 00:40:32,037
His tooth was broken that day, his face was wounded

607
00:40:32,494 --> 00:40:35,381
and his helmet was crushed onto his head

608
00:40:36,695 --> 00:40:40,489
It was Ibn Qamia(ابن قميه) who shot Rasool Allah ﷺ at the cheek

609
00:40:40,945 --> 00:40:47,474
and it was Ut'ba Ibn Abi Waqas(عتبة بن أبي وقاص), who hit the lip and lower tooth of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

610
00:40:47,514 --> 00:40:48,623
Abdul Razzak(عبد الرزاق) says

611
00:40:49,256 --> 00:40:54,411
The Messenger of Allah spoke a curse against Ut'ba Bin Abi Waqas(عتبة بن أبي وقاص) saying

612
00:40:54,753 --> 00:41:00,136
O Allah may change not come to him, so that he does die as an unbeliever

613
00:41:00,656 --> 00:41:04,785
Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير) commented, and no change did come over him

614
00:41:05,098 --> 00:41:09,806
 so that he did die as an unbeliever bound for hellfire

615
00:41:11,644 --> 00:41:14,692
So, what was the reaction to this defeat?

616
00:41:15,639 --> 00:41:21,725
Rasool Allah ﷺ as narrated by Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنه, he said;

617
00:41:22,640 --> 00:41:27,001
While Rasool Allah ﷺ was wiping the blood off his face

618
00:41:27,477 --> 00:41:30,731
He said, "How could any people prosper,

619
00:41:31,183 --> 00:41:34,857
Who struck their prophet and broke his front teeth

620
00:41:35,408 --> 00:41:37,114
while he call people to Allah.?

621
00:41:37,875 --> 00:41:39,335
How could these people prosper?

622
00:41:39,864 --> 00:41:41,007
How could they succeed?

623
00:41:41,713 --> 00:41:45,296
When they do this to the Prophet who's calling them to Allahعزوجل

624
00:41:46,563 --> 00:41:48,501
Allahعزوجل revealed the Ayaah(آية).

625
00:41:49,021 --> 00:41:58,478
لَيْسَ لَكَ مِنَ الْأَمْرِ شَيْءٌ أَوْ يَتُوبَ عَلَيْهِمْ أَوْ يُعَذِّبَهُمْ فَإِنَّهُمْ ظَالِمُونَ۝

626
00:41:59,195 --> 00:42:03,191
Not for you or Muhammad(محمد) but for Allah is the decision

627
00:42:03,587 --> 00:42:07,712
whether he should cut them down, or forgive them or punish them.

628
00:42:08,046 --> 00:42:09,287
For indeed, they are wrongdoers.

629
00:42:09,340 --> 00:42:12,346
So, Allahعزوجل is saying the fate of these people is not up to you.

630
00:42:13,345 --> 00:42:14,907
It's in the hands of Allahعزوجل

631
00:42:15,444 --> 00:42:19,743
It is up to Allahعزوجل to cut them down or to forgive them or to punish them

632
00:42:20,290 --> 00:42:23,542
They deserve punishment but if Allahعزوجل wants to forgive them

633
00:42:23,721 --> 00:42:24,674
It is up to Him

634
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:31,507
So, this shows you that even Rasool Allah ﷺ does not control the fate of humanity.

635
00:42:31,587 --> 00:42:33,478
 It's all in the hands of Allahعزوجل

636
00:42:34,082 --> 00:42:37,418
Allahعزوجل is the One, who controls who becomes a Muslim and who doesn't

637
00:42:37,498 --> 00:42:39,959
 and who should be punished and who shouldn't be punished.

638
00:42:40,039 --> 00:42:42,638
 So, if this right wasn't given to Rasool Allah ﷺ

639
00:42:42,993 --> 00:42:44,525
who are we to claim that right.

640
00:42:44,704 --> 00:42:46,379
It's all in the hands of Allahعزوجل.

641
00:42:47,972 --> 00:42:53,020
Some of the Muslims, when they saw the defeat,

642
00:42:53,100 --> 00:42:56,639
and when they heard the rumor that Rasool Allah ﷺ was killed

643
00:42:56,679 --> 00:43:01,209
because this rumor spread like wildfire in the Muslim army that he was killed.

644
00:43:01,494 --> 00:43:04,669
The origin of the rumor was that he was injured.

645
00:43:05,217 --> 00:43:09,032
But you know, in such a state things could get blown out of proportion.

646
00:43:09,111 --> 00:43:13,756
 So, the rumor that was going around was that Rasool Allah ﷺ was in fact killed.

647
00:43:14,152 --> 00:43:16,351
So, how did they react to that

648
00:43:16,888 --> 00:43:18,206
Well, some of them said;

649
00:43:18,707 --> 00:43:21,447
We'd better send an envoy to Abdullah Bin Obaey,

650
00:43:21,586 --> 00:43:23,820
and have him get us a truce from Abu Sufiyan

651
00:43:24,225 --> 00:43:26,327
People Muhammad has been killed

652
00:43:26,718 --> 00:43:29,662
Go back home before they get to you and kill you.

653
00:43:30,527 --> 00:43:33,742
Here we have some Muslims, who were defeated

654
00:43:34,348 --> 00:43:36,076
the defeat reached to their hearts

655
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:40,183
 And under the pressure of the moment

656
00:43:41,841 --> 00:43:47,581
They thought that the best course of action was to go to Abdullah Bin Obaey, the Munafiq(منافق)

657
00:43:48,149 --> 00:43:53,987
because he has good relations with Quraish and to ask him to bring a truce

658
00:43:55,059 --> 00:43:59,009
and Subhaan Allah(سبحان الله) Yani(يعني) The Battle of Uhud(أحد) itself may not repeat

659
00:43:59,534 --> 00:44:02,965
but the reaction of the people can repeat in events that are similar.

660
00:44:03,486 --> 00:44:06,938
So, sometimes you find that when Muslims are under pressure and

661
00:44:07,271 --> 00:44:12,779
 when they feel that they could be defeated in battle.

662
00:44:13,494 --> 00:44:15,589
You can have some people who would now think

663
00:44:15,788 --> 00:44:19,173
Well, why don't I go to the government's and ask them to help me

664
00:44:19,213 --> 00:44:23,316
 or why don't I go to the enemies of Allahعزوجل and let's have a truce with them.

665
00:44:23,641 --> 00:44:25,023
 This is a sign of weakness.

666
00:44:25,614 --> 00:44:28,824
But The Muslims who had strong Eeman(ايمان) in their heart.

667
00:44:28,864 --> 00:44:30,000
What was their reaction?

668
00:44:30,909 --> 00:44:34,000
One of Al-Muhajiroon(ألمهاجرون) said that he passed by one of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار)

669
00:44:35,063 --> 00:44:39,267
a man who was covered in his own blood, He was soaked in his own blood and he asked him

670
00:44:39,555 --> 00:44:41,826
Are you aware that Muhammad(محمد), has been killed

671
00:44:42,192 --> 00:44:45,569
The Ansaari(أنصاري) responded: If Muhammad has been killed

672
00:44:45,921 --> 00:44:48,576
Then he must have fulfilled his mission.

673
00:44:48,759 --> 00:44:50,560
 So fight on for your religion

674
00:44:50,799 --> 00:44:53,964
Let's die as he died fighting for Islam

675
00:44:55,036 --> 00:44:58,575
So, these are Muslims, who cannot be defeated in their hearts,

676
00:44:58,739 --> 00:45:00,426
 even if they're defeated on the battleground.

677
00:45:01,906 --> 00:45:04,152
Defeat will never get into their spirit

678
00:45:04,687 --> 00:45:09,904
they will always have commitment and this is what, in Islam is called Thabaat(ثبات), steadfast

679
00:45:10,716 --> 00:45:16,633
Never was such a Muslim, try to negotiate with the enemy of Allahعزوجل

680
00:45:16,673 --> 00:45:18,412
 or ask the Munafiqeen(منافقين)

681
00:45:19,437 --> 00:45:22,619
So, we are employees with Allah, we're working for Allahعزوجل

682
00:45:23,547 --> 00:45:25,921
and reward from Allah was our due.

683
00:45:26,135 --> 00:45:29,465
We're doing this and expecting the reward to come from Allahعزوجل.

684
00:45:29,825 --> 00:45:35,119
Some of us passed away or left without enjoying any part of their reward.

685
00:45:35,230 --> 00:45:39,451
 Some of us, died before receiving any of their payments from Allah

686
00:45:39,905 --> 00:45:42,254
Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير) was one of these.

687
00:45:42,987 --> 00:45:46,884
He was killed at the Battle of Uhud(أحَد), leaving nothing but the cloak.

688
00:45:48,027 --> 00:45:51,485
When we covered his head with it, His feet emerged.

689
00:45:52,177 --> 00:45:55,262
When his feet were covered with it, his head emerged.

690
00:45:55,837 --> 00:45:58,479
And so the Prophet told us cover his head with it

691
00:45:58,799 --> 00:46:01,964
and place Izkhar(إزخر) some plant over his feet.

692
00:46:03,364 --> 00:46:06,039
And then he talks about the current condition, now.

693
00:46:06,079 --> 00:46:11,807
he said, some of us have their fruit already ripened, and they are harvesting them.

694
00:46:12,886 --> 00:46:17,020
Some of us are receiving the payment for their good in Duniya(دنيا)

695
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:19,617
while some of us are going to receive it in full in Aakhirah(آخرة).

696
00:46:20,118 --> 00:46:26,550
So he's saying that people like Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير) who died with nothing, and didn't see the victory of Islam

697
00:46:26,775 --> 00:46:29,641
and see the world opening its gates to us,

698
00:46:30,014 --> 00:46:33,751
they are the ones who will receive their payment in full on the day of judgment from Allah

699
00:46:34,072 --> 00:46:39,233
but people like us are now harvesting some of their fruits in Duniya(دنيا).

700
00:46:39,727 --> 00:46:41,784
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf رضي الله عنه said,

701
00:46:41,849 --> 00:46:44,188
Mus'ab(مصعب) was killed, yet he was better than me.

702
00:46:44,719 --> 00:46:47,332
Let me go back, this is also mentioned in Al-Bukhari(البخاريْ),

703
00:46:47,571 --> 00:46:49,536
Food was brought to Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبد الرحمن ابن عوف)

704
00:46:49,645 --> 00:46:53,100
and Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبد الرحمن ابن عوف) was the millionaire of the Sahabah(صحابه), he was the wealthiest among them.

705
00:46:53,418 --> 00:46:55,147
So they brought him this nice food

706
00:46:56,410 --> 00:46:59,322
and when he saw the food he said,

707
00:46:59,639 --> 00:47:02,160
Mus'ab(مصعب) was killed yet he was better than me.

708
00:47:02,587 --> 00:47:04,869
A cloak was used as his shroud

709
00:47:05,367 --> 00:47:07,963
Hamza(حمزة) was killed, yet he was better than me.

710
00:47:08,334 --> 00:47:11,524
While we have been granted earthly favors.

711
00:47:12,302 --> 00:47:15,304
He then wept until his food was cold.

712
00:47:17,236 --> 00:47:25,191
Rasool Allah ﷺ came and stood over Mus'ab Ibn Umair رضي الله عنه

713
00:47:25,711 --> 00:47:28,534
and he recited the Ayaah(آية)

714
00:47:28,843 --> 00:47:36,188
مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ رِجَالٌ صَدَقُوا مَا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ عَلَيْهِ ۖ

715
00:47:36,784 --> 00:47:43,971
فَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ قَضَىٰ نَحْبَهُ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ يَنْتَظِرُ ۖ

716
00:47:44,479 --> 00:47:48,166
Among the believers are men true to what they promised Allah,

717
00:47:49,059 --> 00:47:52,175
among them is he who has fulfilled his vow,

718
00:47:52,676 --> 00:47:55,459
and among them is he, who awaits his chance.

719
00:47:55,876 --> 00:47:59,309
And they did not alter the terms of their commitments by any alteration.

720
00:48:00,531 --> 00:48:03,500
So, this Ayaah(آية) means that we have a covenant with Allah.

721
00:48:04,068 --> 00:48:06,613
Some people fulfilled that vow and they died

722
00:48:07,446 --> 00:48:12,265
and an example of that is Mus'ab Ibn Umair رضي الله عنه.

723
00:48:14,287 --> 00:48:19,649
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said: I bear witness that these are Shuhadah(شهداء)

724
00:48:20,476 --> 00:48:21,914
so come and visit them.

725
00:48:22,303 --> 00:48:28,130
In the name of Who's, my soul is in His hands anyone who gives them Salaam(سلام) up to the Day of Judgment

726
00:48:28,698 --> 00:48:30,645
they would respond back to it.

727
00:48:31,050 --> 00:48:35,923
And this is Hassan(حسن) narration, narrated by Haakim رضي الله عنه.

728
00:48:38,537 --> 00:48:41,287
Sa'ad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد ابن ربيعة), one of the leaders of Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار),

729
00:48:41,398 --> 00:48:45,699
 Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to know what happened to him.

730
00:48:46,136 --> 00:48:50,225
So, he said, who will find out for me, what became of Sa'ad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعدبن ربيعة)

731
00:48:50,575 --> 00:48:52,344
whether he is alive or dead?

732
00:48:52,939 --> 00:48:57,429
So, one of the Ansaar(أنْصَار), went looking for him,

733
00:48:58,304 --> 00:49:02,595
and he came and Sa'ad(سعد) was in his last moments.

734
00:49:04,591 --> 00:49:08,991
So, he said that Rasool Allah ﷺ sent me to you to see, how are you?

735
00:49:09,031 --> 00:49:10,069
 Are you dead or alive.?

736
00:49:10,252 --> 00:49:11,179
Sa'ad(سعد) said,

737
00:49:11,841 --> 00:49:15,120
Listen carefully to his words, this is one of the leaders of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار)

738
00:49:15,697 --> 00:49:23,065
somebody who's dying, because, of giving refuge to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

739
00:49:23,827 --> 00:49:24,650
He said,

740
00:49:25,474 --> 00:49:26,724
I am among the dead.

741
00:49:27,335 --> 00:49:29,766
Inform the Messenger of Allah of this.

742
00:49:30,499 --> 00:49:32,639
Sa'ad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد ابن ربيعة) says to you,

743
00:49:32,940 --> 00:49:40,935
May Allah reward you on our account better than He ever rewarded any Prophet, on account of his nation

744
00:49:42,397 --> 00:49:44,960
and greet your people from me and tell them,

745
00:49:45,434 --> 00:49:47,406
Sa'ad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد ابن ربيعة) says to you

746
00:49:47,875 --> 00:49:52,659
you will find no excuse with Allah, if harm comes to your Prophet

747
00:49:53,190 --> 00:49:55,706
while you still have one eye to blink.

748
00:49:57,423 --> 00:50:02,146
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked this man to go and check out the status of Sa'ad Ibn Rabiyyah(سعد ابن ربيعة)

749
00:50:02,186 --> 00:50:03,569
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ told him,

750
00:50:04,013 --> 00:50:06,575
If you find him alive give him my Salaam(سلام).

751
00:50:07,328 --> 00:50:11,313
So, the man comes to Sa'ad(سعد) and said, Rasool Allah ﷺ delivers his Salaam(سلام) to you.

752
00:50:11,871 --> 00:50:14,901
So, Sa'ad is telling to Rasool Allah ﷺ, he is giving Rasool Ullah a message

753
00:50:14,952 --> 00:50:16,353
and he's giving his people a message.

754
00:50:16,385 --> 00:50:18,527
So, these are his last words in Duniyah(دنيا)

755
00:50:19,046 --> 00:50:23,993
He is saying may Allah reward Rasool Allah ﷺ better than he rewarded any other Prophet.

756
00:50:24,622 --> 00:50:27,490
He's saying this before he dies

757
00:50:29,367 --> 00:50:32,061
and he's asking Allah to reward Muhammadﷺ,

758
00:50:32,101 --> 00:50:35,741
even though it was because of Muhammadﷺ that he is now dying.

759
00:50:36,322 --> 00:50:38,106
So, these Muslims of today

760
00:50:38,512 --> 00:50:43,590
who are so stingy and not willing to give up their lives or their wealth for Allahعَزّوجَلّ

761
00:50:43,891 --> 00:50:45,960
and if any harm would come to them

762
00:50:46,249 --> 00:50:48,097
and they think it's because of Islam.

763
00:50:48,331 --> 00:50:52,794
They would be willing to compromise in their religion just to protect their Duniya(دنيا).

764
00:50:53,326 --> 00:50:56,804
Compare that to these Sahabah رضي الله عنهم these Ansaar(انصار)

765
00:50:57,123 --> 00:51:02,553
these Ansaar(انصار), their lives are wrecked, their business is going down,

766
00:51:03,119 --> 00:51:05,299
their farms are not tended to,

767
00:51:05,694 --> 00:51:09,561
their suffering in their families, their children are suffering because of that.

768
00:51:09,970 --> 00:51:13,851
I mean, their entire livelihood is upside down

769
00:51:14,030 --> 00:51:17,466
because of giving refuge to Muhammadﷺ and the Muslims.

770
00:51:18,545 --> 00:51:21,741
And now he's saying: O Allah reward Muhammadﷺ for that

771
00:51:22,048 --> 00:51:26,527
reward him, give him the best reward that You would ever give a Prophet of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

772
00:51:26,838 --> 00:51:31,124
And then he tells his people, who are already dying in the battle, he tells them,

773
00:51:32,252 --> 00:51:37,005
You will find no excuse with Allah, if harm comes to Rasool Allah ﷺ

774
00:51:37,230 --> 00:51:39,130
while you still have one eye to blink.

775
00:51:39,176 --> 00:51:42,303
As long as there is life in you,

776
00:51:42,552 --> 00:51:46,598
you have no excuse if even Rasool Allah ﷺ is pricked with a thorn.

777
00:51:47,760 --> 00:51:52,534
Any pain that Rasool Allah ﷺ feels, while you are still alive, you are to blame.

778
00:51:54,345 --> 00:51:58,405
These are Al-Ansaar(ألأنصار), who gave victory to the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

779
00:51:59,151 --> 00:52:02,001
There upon he died, رضي الله عنه

780
00:52:03,161 --> 00:52:08,315
Abdullah Bin Jahash رضي الله عنه and Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد ابن ابي وقاص),

781
00:52:09,146 --> 00:52:10,631
they met before the battle.

782
00:52:11,457 --> 00:52:14,975
So, Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) said, let's go and make Dua(دعا).

783
00:52:15,587 --> 00:52:19,777
So, they go together, one of them is going to make Dua(دعا) and the other one will say, Ameen(آمين)

784
00:52:20,582 --> 00:52:23,184
Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد ابن ابي وقاص) made his Dua(دعا)

785
00:52:24,025 --> 00:52:27,722
He said: O Allah If I meet the enemy

786
00:52:28,132 --> 00:52:31,183
then enable me to meet a strong fighter.

787
00:52:31,476 --> 00:52:38,180
This is strange, you know, a soldier would usually want to find an easy target somebody weak somebody lame,

788
00:52:38,331 --> 00:52:42,148
Sa'ad says: no, I want to meet a strong fighter, the best of them.

789
00:52:43,125 --> 00:52:47,888
 O Allah, If I meet the enemy then enable me to meet a strong fighter

790
00:52:48,458 --> 00:52:50,458
who will fight me and I will fight him

791
00:52:50,713 --> 00:52:53,039
and then give me victory over him

792
00:52:53,570 --> 00:52:58,653
and enable me to kill him and take his Salb(سلب), take his armor.

793
00:52:59,522 --> 00:53:01,229
Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) said, Ameen(آمين)

794
00:53:02,051 --> 00:53:03,955
Sa'ad told him, it's now your turn to make Dua(دعا).

795
00:53:04,701 --> 00:53:09,648
Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش) said, O Allah enabled me to meet a strong fighter

796
00:53:10,365 --> 00:53:13,151
who would fight me and I would fight him.

797
00:53:13,696 --> 00:53:18,354
And then he would kill me and cut my nose and ear.

798
00:53:18,902 --> 00:53:21,148
So, when I meet You, You will say

799
00:53:21,551 --> 00:53:24,701
why was your ear and nose cut, O Abdallah(عبدالله).?

800
00:53:24,971 --> 00:53:28,066
 I would say for you and your messenger.

801
00:53:28,852 --> 00:53:31,923
And you would say, you are speaking the truth.

802
00:53:32,722 --> 00:53:34,693
Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد ابن ابي وقاص) said: Ameen(آمين)

803
00:53:35,619 --> 00:53:38,697
Sa'ad(سعد) was narrating the story to his son.

804
00:53:38,737 --> 00:53:44,426
And he said, Oh, my son, the Dua(دعا) of AbdAllah(عبدالله) was better than mine.

805
00:53:45,051 --> 00:53:50,633
By the end of the day, I saw his nose and ear tied to a string.

806
00:53:51,504 --> 00:53:54,276
Allah did accept the Dua(دعا) of Abdullah Bin Jahash(عبدالله بن جحش)

807
00:53:54,817 --> 00:53:58,286
and he did meet a strong man, who fought him and killed him

808
00:53:58,949 --> 00:54:03,927
and then, his body was mutilated, and his nose was cut and his ears were cut

809
00:54:04,222 --> 00:54:06,374
and there they were tied in a string

810
00:54:06,739 --> 00:54:08,889
and Sa'ad(سعد) saw that string with his own eyes.

811
00:54:10,381 --> 00:54:12,053
This Dua(دعا) shows that

812
00:54:12,853 --> 00:54:17,486
it is allowed to ask Allah to give you death,

813
00:54:18,129 --> 00:54:20,986
if it is in his path, if it is Fee-Sabeel-Lillah(فِي سَبيل الله)

814
00:54:21,989 --> 00:54:31,154
Another amazing story of a Shaheed(شهيد) was that of Abdullah Bin Haraam رضي الله عنه,

815
00:54:31,515 --> 00:54:35,010
or actually I mentioned the story of Khaisamah(خيثمة),

816
00:54:35,404 --> 00:54:38,240
and this was narrated by Ibn Al-Qayyim(إبن قيم) in Zaad Al-Ma'ad(زاد المعاد).

817
00:54:38,857 --> 00:54:45,832
Khaisamah(خيثمة) was an old man, but he still wanted to join and fight and we know that old men are excused.

818
00:54:46,848 --> 00:54:50,054
 Khaisamah(خيثمة), his son died as a Shaheed(شهيد) on Badr(بدر).

819
00:54:50,378 --> 00:54:53,127
So, he said I missed the Battle of Badr(بدر)

820
00:54:53,442 --> 00:54:55,366
and I was so eager to join,

821
00:54:55,533 --> 00:55:00,964
but me and my son drew lots and he went and was awarded with martyrdom.

822
00:55:01,579 --> 00:55:04,736
So, one of them stayed behind, so they cast lots,

823
00:55:04,856 --> 00:55:09,139
and it came out that Khaisamah(خيثمة) has to stay and his son has to go.

824
00:55:10,336 --> 00:55:14,146
Khaisamah(خيثمة) then said, I saw him last night in my sleep.

825
00:55:14,757 --> 00:55:18,608
He looked great and was enjoying the fruits of Jannah(جنة).

826
00:55:19,132 --> 00:55:22,688
He told me come and be our companion in paradise.

827
00:55:23,069 --> 00:55:25,338
I have found what Allah promise me to be true.

828
00:55:26,526 --> 00:55:27,819
So, O Messenger of Allah,

829
00:55:28,641 --> 00:55:32,117
I swear to Allah, I am so eager to join him in Jannah(جنة)

830
00:55:33,209 --> 00:55:35,448
I am old and my bones are soft.

831
00:55:36,047 --> 00:55:41,348
So, ask Allah, O Messenger of Allah to award me Shahadah(شهادة) and allow me to join Sa'ad(سعد) in Jannah(جنة).

832
00:55:41,716 --> 00:55:43,129
Khaisamah(خيثمة) is saying, I'm getting old,

833
00:55:43,314 --> 00:55:46,760
I'm missing the train, I'm afraid that if I don't die as a Shaheed(شهيد) now

834
00:55:47,104 --> 00:55:48,468
I might end up dying on my bed.

835
00:55:49,575 --> 00:55:52,375
So, O messenger of Allah make Dua(دعا) that I die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

836
00:55:53,259 --> 00:55:55,949
I want to meet my son, I want to join him in Jannah(جنه).

837
00:55:56,755 --> 00:56:02,043
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did make Dua(دعا) for him and he did die as a shaheed رضي الله عنه.

838
00:56:03,563 --> 00:56:05,241
Wahb Al-Muzani(وهب المزني),

839
00:56:05,897 --> 00:56:09,424
these are not from Madina, but they're from outside, from a tribe called Muzaina(مزينه).

840
00:56:09,995 --> 00:56:15,336
He and his relative were shepherds and they came to Madina with their sheep

841
00:56:16,101 --> 00:56:17,717
and they came to find Madina empty.

842
00:56:17,757 --> 00:56:19,107
They said, Where is everyone?

843
00:56:19,622 --> 00:56:22,865
They said they went to fight with Rasool Allah ﷺ at the Battle of Uhud(أحد).

844
00:56:23,198 --> 00:56:27,076
 So, they left their sheep and they went to join the battle.

845
00:56:27,736 --> 00:56:30,222
They came while the Muslims were winning, they joined in.

846
00:56:30,587 --> 00:56:32,198
But then when the tides returning

847
00:56:33,130 --> 00:56:34,169
they carried on the fight,

848
00:56:34,209 --> 00:56:36,328
they didn't just join because the Muslims were winning,

849
00:56:36,368 --> 00:56:38,701
they were also fighting with the Muslims, when they were being defeated.

850
00:56:38,960 --> 00:56:41,733
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a group approaching them

851
00:56:42,068 --> 00:56:44,535
and he said, Who will take care of this group.

852
00:56:44,825 --> 00:56:46,202
So, Al-Muzzani(المزني) said: I will,

853
00:56:46,282 --> 00:56:47,455
Wahb(وهب) said, I will.

854
00:56:47,771 --> 00:56:49,897
So, he advances and attacks them.

855
00:56:50,493 --> 00:56:52,644
And he pushes them back.

856
00:56:53,300 --> 00:56:56,707
A second group comes in and Rasool Allah ﷺ asks for volunteers

857
00:56:56,749 --> 00:56:58,542
Al-Muzzani(المزني) goes again and volunteers

858
00:56:58,565 --> 00:57:01,282
and he stops them and pushes them back.

859
00:57:01,744 --> 00:57:05,380
The third time, he also stands up so this time, Rasool Allah ﷺ said,

860
00:57:05,676 --> 00:57:08,735
Go and receive the glad tidings of Jannah(جنة)

861
00:57:09,656 --> 00:57:16,409
So, he went into fight, and he was throwing himself in the middle of this group,

862
00:57:16,449 --> 00:57:19,434
 and then he would come out and attack again and come out and attack again.

863
00:57:19,704 --> 00:57:22,785
Rasool Allah ﷺ was watching that and he would say, O, Allah: Yarham(يرحم)

864
00:57:23,111 --> 00:57:24,336
O Allah have mercy on him.

865
00:57:24,440 --> 00:57:27,379
Rasool Ullah was making Dua(دعا) for Wahb Al-Muzzani(وهب المزني)

866
00:57:27,881 --> 00:57:33,429
and he continued doing this until these swords shredded him and he was killed.

867
00:57:34,048 --> 00:57:38,691
By the way, when they found his body,

868
00:57:38,731 --> 00:57:41,806
He had 20 injuries all of them were fatal injuries

869
00:57:42,316 --> 00:57:44,643
and Umar Bin Khattab رضي الله عنه said;

870
00:57:44,941 --> 00:57:47,412
that is the best death I could wish for.

871
00:57:47,798 --> 00:57:49,038
That's how I want to die.

872
00:57:49,720 --> 00:57:53,409
Look at those injuries and every one of them is fatal and he was still fighting.

873
00:57:54,884 --> 00:57:58,724
Sa'ad Ibn Abi Waqas(سعد ابن ابي وقاص) after the Battle of Al-Qadisiyya(القادسيه)

874
00:57:59,332 --> 00:58:03,002
was approached by a man from Muzaina(مزينه), his name is Bilal(بلال)

875
00:58:03,395 --> 00:58:09,565
because, one of his relatives didn't get his share of the booty.

876
00:58:09,866 --> 00:58:12,422
 So, they went to visit Sa'ad(سعد).

877
00:58:12,668 --> 00:58:17,784
 So, Sa'ad(سعد) asked this man he said, Are you a relative of Wahb Al-Muzzani(وهب المزني)?

878
00:58:17,849 --> 00:58:20,202
 He said: yes, I'm his nephew.

879
00:58:21,199 --> 00:58:24,767
So, Sa'ad, said, and this is years later, this is 13 years later

880
00:58:25,029 --> 00:58:26,822
Sa'ad(سعد) is still remembering that day.

881
00:58:26,862 --> 00:58:27,547
 He said;

882
00:58:27,841 --> 00:58:32,268
On that day, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was asking for volunteers to go and stop this group.

883
00:58:32,474 --> 00:58:35,395
 It was your uncle who was attacking them all the time.

884
00:58:35,651 --> 00:58:37,863
The third time, I went to join him

885
00:58:38,965 --> 00:58:41,779
because I wanted to receive the same reward that he would receive

886
00:58:41,859 --> 00:58:45,431
 because I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say, you receive the glad tidings of Jannah.

887
00:58:45,471 --> 00:58:46,451
  اَبْشِرْ بِالْجَنَّةْ

888
00:58:46,615 --> 00:58:48,416
So, Sa'ad(سعد) said, I went with him

889
00:58:48,921 --> 00:58:51,236
and he mentioned how brave and courageous

890
00:58:51,645 --> 00:58:53,306
Wahb(وهب) was until, he was killed.

891
00:58:54,267 --> 00:58:57,941
Sa'ad(سعد) said, No state of death would I love to meet Allah with

892
00:58:58,247 --> 00:59:00,231
more than the state of death of that was Al-Muzzani(المزني).

893
00:59:00,768 --> 00:59:02,973
That's the best way to die.

894
00:59:03,187 --> 00:59:04,320
Sa'ad(سعد) said;

895
00:59:04,727 --> 00:59:06,966
When he was killed after the battle was over.

896
00:59:07,252 --> 00:59:12,338
I saw Rasool Allah ﷺ go and stand on top of his grave when they were digging it

897
00:59:13,032 --> 00:59:16,206
and waiting right there, until the burial was over,

898
00:59:16,258 --> 00:59:18,391
 even though Rasool Allah ﷺ was exhausted.

899
00:59:18,895 --> 00:59:22,336
Rasool Allah was injured and he was tired and he could barely stand up.

900
00:59:22,610 --> 00:59:27,042
But he nevertheless stood up, on his grave, until he was buried.

901
00:59:28,839 --> 00:59:31,883
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said, may Allah be pleased with him

902
00:59:32,265 --> 00:59:33,771
because I am pleased with him.

903
00:59:35,159 --> 00:59:39,667
O Allah, be pleased with him because I am pleased with him.

904
00:59:40,262 --> 00:59:43,461
Amr Bin Jammooh(عمرو بن جموح) another Shaheed(شهيد).

905
00:59:44,445 --> 00:59:46,563
Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) narrates;

906
00:59:46,864 --> 00:59:48,505
My father related to me,

907
00:59:48,545 --> 00:59:50,645
he is mentioning this, in the book of Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق)

908
00:59:50,792 --> 00:59:54,050
My father related to me from elders of Bannu Salamah(بنوسلمه), who said;

909
00:59:54,612 --> 00:59:58,555
Amr Bin Jammooh(عمرو بن جموح), was a man exceedingly lame.

910
00:59:59,202 --> 01:00:04,159
He had four sons who fought battles like lions alongside the Messenger of Allah.

911
01:00:05,012 --> 01:00:06,838
When it came time for the Battle of Uhud(أحَد).

912
01:00:07,325 --> 01:00:10,759
They wanted to restrain Amr(عمرو) saying that Allah has excused him.

913
01:00:11,674 --> 01:00:13,420
So, he went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said,

914
01:00:13,460 --> 01:00:16,653
My sons want to restrain me from going to battle with you.

915
01:00:17,109 --> 01:00:21,634
But by Allah, I want to step this lame foot of mine into Paradise.

916
01:00:23,079 --> 01:00:25,943
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him it's not obliged to you to fight

917
01:00:26,256 --> 01:00:28,451
because you're lame, Aaraj(اعرج), you don't have to fight.

918
01:00:28,949 --> 01:00:31,259
But then Rasool Allahﷺ told his sons,

919
01:00:31,497 --> 01:00:35,251
it is not your duty to restrain him, if he wants to fight let him go.

920
01:00:35,483 --> 01:00:38,286
Allah might well grant him martyrdom and he did die as a Shaheed(شهيد).

921
01:00:38,762 --> 01:00:41,992
So, we learn from this that even if a person is excused from fighting,

922
01:00:42,273 --> 01:00:46,735
it is allowed for him to fight. If it's not obligatory on him, he can still fight.

923
01:00:47,118 --> 01:00:49,866
We know that the blind man has fought in battles,

924
01:00:50,086 --> 01:00:52,319
we know that lame men have fought in battles,

925
01:00:52,359 --> 01:00:56,184
we know that people who are have other diseases did fight in battle.

926
01:00:56,224 --> 01:01:01,326
So, it's allowed for a person who is excused from fighting to join in and fight.

927
01:01:02,157 --> 01:01:08,858
This also shows you how eager the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم were to die as Shaheeds(شهيد).

928
01:01:09,863 --> 01:01:12,500
We'll stop here and carry on In Sha Allah Ta'ala(ان شاء الله تعالى) tomorrow

929
01:01:12,894 --> 01:01:15,484
with some other stories of Ash-Shuhadaa(الشهدآء)

930
01:01:15,891 --> 01:01:19,231
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ

931
01:01:19,560 --> 01:01:21,705
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

